Zammad is installed under /srv/www/zammad. The web server document root
is public/. Configuration is /etc/zammad/zammad.env and
/etc/zammad/database.yml. Attachments, cache and temporary files are
under /var/lib/zammad. Logs are under /var/log/zammad.

The package creates a local PostgreSQL database and starts Zammad.
Puma listens on 127.0.0.1:3000 and the websocket server on
127.0.0.1:6042. Neither is meant to be reached directly from other
machines. Redis is a private instance, redis@zammad, on
/run/redis/zammad/redis.sock.

Database access uses the PostgreSQL socket as the OS user "zammad"
(peer authentication, empty password, no host in database.yml). A
freshly initialised OpenMandriva cluster does this. If local sockets
on this host require a password, set it in /etc/zammad/database.yml
and run:

  systemctl restart zammad.service

1. Enable a web server site. The package does not listen on port 80
   by itself.

   nginx:

     ln -s ../sites-available/zammad.conf /etc/nginx/sites-enabled/zammad.conf
     systemctl enable --now nginx
     systemctl reload nginx

   The server name is zammad.* (for example http://zammad.example.com/).
   Point that name at this machine. It does not replace the default
   nginx site.

   Apache:

     cp /etc/httpd/conf/vhosts.d/zammad.conf.disabled \
        /etc/httpd/conf/vhosts.d/zammad.conf
     edit ServerName in that file
     systemctl enable --now httpd-prefork
     systemctl reload httpd-prefork

   The first Apache VirtualHost becomes the default server for port 80.
   Set ServerName before reloading, or this vhost answers every name.
   The packaged vhost grants access to every client. Puma itself stays
   on 127.0.0.1.

2. Open the site and finish the setup wizard (administrator, organisation,
   email). The wizard is the initial login. There is no default password.

3. Optional AI reply. This is off. When it is on, a new customer
   message is sent to a local model. If the model reports a confidence
   of at least 10 percent, Zammad replies on the same channel with the
   text in /etc/zammad/ai-reply.template. A lower confidence sends
   nothing. Phone, chat, fax, and X messages are skipped. A web form
   message is answered by email when the customer and the group both
   have an email address.

   Edit /etc/zammad/ai-reply.conf. Set ENABLED=1 and AI_MODEL. The
   default server is Ollama at http://127.0.0.1:11434, and the model
   has to be pulled already. The next message uses the saved file.
   Restarting Zammad is not required.

   Placeholders in the template: {{response}} {{ticket_number}}
   {{customer_name}} {{subject}}.

   A URL ending in /v1 is treated as OpenAI chat completions. For
   hosted SpaceXAI, set AI_BASE_URL=https://api.x.ai/v1 and
   AI_MODEL=grok-4.7, and put the key in AI_API_KEY in the same file.
   That file is readable by root and the zammad group. Do not put the
   key in zammad.env, which is world-readable. An empty AI_API_KEY
   falls back to XAI_API_KEY or AI_API_KEY in the worker environment.

   Zammad's SMS driver sends the first 160 characters only. A long
   template is cut off on SMS. The ticket still stores the full reply.

Elasticsearch is optional. Zammad searches in PostgreSQL without it.
Elasticsearch is not packaged in OpenMandriva.

PGP email needs gnupg, which is recommended but not required.

Commands:

  zammad rake db:migrate
  zammad run rails runner 'Locale.sync; Translation.sync'

Removing the package stops the services and keeps the database and
/var/lib/zammad.
